From d93deec262897b397d1ab5ce06cde3efde8d377f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ni Cunshu <nicunshu@huawei.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Mar 2026 14:14:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 922/960] downstream: mm/filemap: restrict pagecache to
 non-cpuless NUMA nodes

Add a new sysctl vm.filemap_alloc_local to restrict pagecache allocations
to non-cpuless NUMA nodes only, excluding cpuless NUMA nodes within the
current cpuset mems_allowed range.

When enabled, pagecache allocations use round-robin interleaving across
local nodes only, preventing pagecache from being allocated on cpuless
NUMA nodes that may have higher access latency.

The implementation uses seqlock protection (read_mems_allowed_begin/
read_mems_allowed_retry) to handle concurrent modifications of
mems_allowed by cpuset, following the same pattern used in cpuset's
page allocation path.

Reuses current->cpuset_mem_spread_rotor for per-task round-robin node
selection, but restricts the rotor to non-cpuless nodes only.

Signed-off-by: Zheng Chuan <zhengchuan@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Ni Cunshu <nicunshu@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: slim6882 <yangjunshuo@huawei.com>
Conflicts:
	mm/internal.h
[ Context conflict. ]
Signed-off-by: Liu Shixin <liushixin2@huawei.com>
